(draft pull request #23, closed and superseded by this service).

Python dependencies (see requirements.txt), installed from PyPI and not vendored:

- PyJWT, © the PyJWT authors, MIT License
- cryptography (installed through PyJWT[crypto]), © the cryptography authors,
  Apache License 2.0 or BSD-3-Clause
- gunicorn, © the Gunicorn authors, MIT License

External components. The Dockerfile in this directory downloads them at build time, each
pinned by checksum, into the published image. They are not part of this repository and are not
covered by the Apache License above:

- Piper command-line engine 2023.11.14-2, https://github.com/rhasspy/piper, © Michael Hansen,
  MIT License. Its release archive also bundles espeak-ng (and libespeak-ng,
  piper-phonemize), © the espeak-ng authors, GNU GPL-3.0-or-later. The image therefore
  redistributes GPL-3.0 components; they run only as a separate process (the `piper`
  executable) and are not linked into this service. Source:
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  Archive SHA-256 a50cb45f355b7af1f6d758c1b360717877ba0a398cc8cbe6d2a7a3a26e225992.
- Voice uk_UA-ukrainian_tts-medium (3 speakers; the service uses the default, `lada`),
  https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices at revision
  5ec43b186ef915a195d3ddbcfd9916e76c503c3f. Dataset: https://github.com/OHF-Voice/voice-datasets,
  CC0 (per the model card), trained from scratch. SHA-256 of the .onnx
  7920419ac5f6fd8b6450520f24b52ed5a319cb53dd018fbcd71c9e079cbac84f, of the .onnx.json
  4e96e72917ca9b94edc77d6ccfee03a73f450ba2fc1ca93c2e562bc014e5aa55.

Changing the engine or the voice means updating the pins here and in the Dockerfile after
auditing the new license, provenance and checksum.
